# Kaggle Benchmarks Model Proxy credentials.
#
# Generate a Kaggle API token at https://www.kaggle.com/settings ("Create New Token"),
# save it to ~/.kaggle/access_token, then run:
#
#     kaggle benchmarks auth -y
#
# This writes MODEL_PROXY_URL / MODEL_PROXY_API_KEY / MODEL_PROXY_EXPIRY_TIME into
# .env automatically. The proxy credential is SHORT-LIVED (expires in ~20-30 minutes)
# -- rerun `kaggle benchmarks auth -y` whenever it expires, no need to regenerate the
# underlying Kaggle API token itself.
#
# After running `auth`, also add these two lines yourself (not written automatically):
LLM_DEFAULT=google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview
LLMS_AVAILABLE=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5@default,deepseek-ai/deepseek-r1-0528,google/gemini-3-flash-preview,google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview,ibm/granite-4.0-h-small,openai/gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17,openai/gpt-oss-120b,qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct
